  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This makes about 12 crepes serving 4 and takes about 40 minutes including the 30-minute rest. The thing to watch is the heat: the pan needs to be consistently hot enough that a small drop of batter sizzles immediately on contact."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The first crepe is always a test. It tells you if the pan is hot enough and the batter is the right thickness. Adjust from there rather than expecting perfection from the start."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 150,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "whole-milk",
              "amount": 350,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "unsalted-butter",
              "amount": 30,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "melted, plus extra for the pan",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "for sweet crepes",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk together the flour, salt, and sugar if using. Make a well in the centre and crack in the eggs."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk the eggs into the flour, gradually drawing in the flour from the sides."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slowly add the milk, whisking constantly until the batter is smooth and the consistency of single cream. Stir in the melted butter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rest the batter in the fridge for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a 26cm frying pan over medium-high heat. Rub with a small knob of butter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in about 60ml batter and immediately tilt the pan to spread it thinly and evenly across the surface."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook for 60-90 seconds until the edges lift and the underside is golden. Flip with a spatula and cook 30 seconds more. Slide onto a plate."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stack crepes between sheets of baking paper as you go. Serve with lemon and sugar, jam, or savoury fillings."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Crepes tear when flipping",
              "cause": "Flipped too early before the edges lifted, or pan not hot enough",
              "fix": "Wait until the edges are visibly dry and starting to curl before attempting to flip"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Crepes are too thick and more like pancakes",
              "cause": "Too much batter per crepe or batter too thick",
              "fix": "Use less batter per crepe and add a splash more milk to thin the batter"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Batter has lumps",
              "cause": "Milk added too fast or flour not incorporated first",
              "fix": "Whisk eggs into flour first until smooth before adding any milk"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Crepes are eaten all across France but are most closely associated with Brittany in the northwest, where they are a regional staple. The savoury version, made with buckwheat flour, is called a galette. Crepe stalls are common at French markets and street fairs. Crepes Suzette, flambeed in orange liqueur, is the most famous fancy version and remains a fixture of French restaurant theatre."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
